Directors High Level Dashboard Analysis
1. Top Level Performance Metrics (KPIs)
Overview & Purpose
Provides executive leadership with an aggregate summary of Total Revenue, Outpatient Department (OPD) Volume, and Cost Per Visit (CPV) compared against Baseline, Historical, and Target thresholds.

Key Insights
Revenue Exceeds Target: Total Revenue reached 576.37M against a target of 528.39M, achieving an Achievement Rate (ACH%) of 1.09% above expectation and a Growth Rate (G%) of 9.43%.

OPD Volume Target Met: OPD Volume achieved 173.56K compared to a target of 168K (ACH% of 1.04%), representing a slight growth rate (G%) of 0.09%.

Total CPV Dynamics: Actual Cost Per Visit landed at 20.08K, exceeding the set target of 14.73K with a Growth Rate (G%) of 0.75%.

2. Medical Department (MD) Breakdown (Revenue, Volume, & CPV)
Overview & Purpose
Delivers a granular evaluation of individual Medical Departments (e.g., Cath LAB, CCU) segmented by payment payment types (Cash vs. Credit) across primary financial and volume KPIs.

Key Insights
Credit vs. Cash Revenue Disparity: In the Cath LAB department, Credit revenue (23.44M) heavily outpaces Cash revenue (5.10M) out of a total 28.54M MD Revenue.

CCU Payment Structure: CCU generated 11.14M Total Revenue, driven predominantly by Credit payments (10.79M) with minimal Cash contribution (0.35M).

Consolidated Totals Alignment: Total MD metrics reflect aggregate performance, standing at 576.37M Revenue, 173.56K Volume, and 20.08K CPV.

3. Marketing & Patient Acquisition Channels (Digital Marketing vs. Medical CRM)
Overview & Purpose
Compares the performance and efficiency of Digital Marketing initiatives against Medical CRM efforts across Revenue generation, Patient Volume, and acquisition metrics (RPP & CPV).

Key Insights
Revenue Generation: Medical CRM outperformed Digital Marketing in total revenue, generating 74.95M (vs. Target of 83.55M) compared to Digital Marketing's 72.62M (vs. Target of 150.68M).

Digital Marketing Underperformance: Digital Marketing fell significantly short of its revenue target (72.62M Actual vs. 150.68M Target), resulting in a negative Growth Rate (G% of -1.00%).

Volume Conversion: Digital Marketing drove 54K in Volume (exceeding its 47K baseline but under its 110.95K target), while Medical CRM generated 40K in Volume against a 44K target.

Cost Efficiency Metrics: Medical CRM achieved a 20.08K CPV (ACH% of 1.36%), while Digital Marketing recorded an RPP of 12.51K against a target of 12.78K.

Executive Summary & Overall Conclusions (What We Learned Overall)
Overall Revenue Strength: Executive targets were successfully surpassed overall, driven by strong total revenue (576.37M vs. 528.39M target) and steady OPD volume metrics (173.56K vs. 168K target).

Credit Payment Dominance: Operational departments like Cath LAB and CCU exhibit heavy financial dependence on Credit payment models compared to Cash transactions.

Digital Channel Optimization Needed: While Digital Marketing successfully brought in higher volume (54K), it missed its ambitious revenue target by nearly 50%, whereas Medical CRM proved more revenue-efficient relative to its assigned targets.
